{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And I have come down to deliver him</b> — that I revealed myself upon this mountain in fire. This is like the sense of \"and YHWH came down upon Mount Sinai\" (Exodus 19:20), \"because YHWH had come down upon it in fire\" (ibid. 18). Or it is like \"I will go down now and see whether they have done altogether according to the cry that has come to me\" (Genesis 18:21). And I have already explained its secret (ibid. 20)." "<b>unto a land flowing with milk and honey, unto the place of the Canaanite and the Hittite</b> — He mentions here six nations and leaves out the seventh, perhaps because its land was not flowing with milk and honey like these. And so in the verse \"for My angel shall go before you\" (Exodus 23:23) He mentioned these same six. Or perhaps it is a hint that these were conquered first, for they are the ones who gathered together against Joshua, and YHWH delivered them into his hand (Joshua 9:1–2). And our Sages said: the Girgashite departed (Jerusalemite Talmud, Shevi'it 6:1), and therefore he is not mentioned together with those of whom it is said, \"and I will cut them off\" (Exodus 23:23). And so here too He alludes to those who were fought and conquered. I will speak further about this, with HaShem's help (Ramban on Exodus 23:23):<br>And the sense of <b>flowing with milk and honey</b> is that He first praised the land that it is <b>good</b>, to say that its air is good and pleasant for people and every good thing is found in it, and that it is <b>spacious</b>, that all Israel could stand in it in spaciousness. Or the sense of <b>spacious</b> is that it has breadth — lowlands and valleys and great and small plains, and mountains and deep valleys are not its majority. And He turned back and praised it that it is a land of livestock, for there is good pasture in it, and the waters are good, and the milk abounds in the animals, for animals are not healthy and good and abundant in milk except in good air and abundant grass and good water. And because this is found in the meadow and on the heights of mountains, the fruits there are not very rich and fine, He said that it is further <b>rich</b>, that its fruits are rich and sweet, so that the entire land flows with honey from them. And behold, He praised it for all the goodness of HaShem — for grain, for wine, for oil, for flocks and herds. And this is \"it is the beauty of all lands\" (Ezekiel 20:6):<br>And the sense of <b>unto the place of the Canaanite</b> — that He did not say \"unto the land of the Canaanite\" as He says in all other places (Exodus 3:17) — is to hint that they will dispossess them and cut them off and dwell in their place, not that they will be dwelling among them as their fathers did."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The phrase 'its secret' refers back to Ramban's kabbalistic comments on Genesis 18:21 in his commentary there; it is left cryptic per the translator's mandate.", 1 "The citation 'ibid. 17' refers to Exodus 3:17 (להלן י\"ז), i.e., later in the same chapter. The cross-reference '(רמב\"ן על שמות כ\"ג:כ\"ה)' appears to cite verse 23 but the standard enumeration is 23:23; resolved to 23:23 based on the content and the repeated citations of that verse throughout the comment."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:31.180422700Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}